abstract:
The potential role of the IGF-1 system in modulation of longevity is discussed, hypothesizing that the endocrine and metabolic adaptation observed in centenarians and in mammals during caloric restriction may be a physiological strategy for extending lifespan through a slower cell growing/metabolism, a better physiologic reserve capacity, and a shift of cellular metabolism from cell proliferation to repair activities.Expand
